  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tackling Serious and Organized Corruption (TSOC)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Malawi):  Tackling Serious and Organized Corruption (TSOC) supports Malawian law enforcement to increase the likelihood and severity of sanction for serious and organized corruption. This activity strengthens technical capacity and interagency coordination among key law enforcement agencies, including the Anti Corruption Bureau, Director of Public Prosecutions, Financial Intelligence Agency, and the Malawi Police Service, to detect, investigate, and prosecute strategic corruption cases..TSOC will increase the risks of engaging in corruption and strengthen systems that regulate the movement of money and services through the economy, by supporting efforts to publicly expose corrupt individuals and corporations; seize and recover assets linked to corruption and other serious crimes; as well as improve strategic case work and conviction rates. Working through embedded technical assistance, TSOC will increase the practical skills and working knowledge of law enforcement agencies, to address obstacles that impede effective prosecution of corruption and public fraud cases. The activity will also support a range of prevention activities that engage non-state actors, including media, civil society, and the private sector, to implement anti-corruption and accountability activities. These include investigative journalism, advocacy for greater transparency in the business environment, and advocacy for greater parliamentary scrutiny of government spending..TSOC contributes to Malawi&apos;s Integrated Country Strategy (ICS) Goal 1: Democratic and Accountable Governance; and Objective 1.1: Support Malawian institutions, including parliament, the judiciary, and accountability institutions, to make governance more effective, transparent, and accountable. It also supports the Mission&apos;s CDCS (2020 - 2025) Development Objective 1, which seeks to improve public sector effectiveness and accountability at the national and decentralized levels.</narrative>
  </description>
